  "ingredients": [
    "1/2 medium onion (diced)",
    "1 tablespoon fresh garlic (minced)",
    "2 medium zucchini",
    "1 teaspoon paprika",
    "1/2 teaspoon crushed red pepper flakes",
    "1 teaspoon dried oregano",
    "salt and pepper",
    "16 ounce ground pork",
    "1 cup cheddar cheese (shredded)",
    "1/2 cup chicken broth"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 350F. Cut the zucchini in half, length wise.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-zucchini-boats/#wprm-recipe-52389-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/11/sausage-stuffed-zucchini-boats-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using a spoon or melon baller, scoop out the zucchini so it becomes a shell for the fillings. Chop up the zucchini that you scooped out of the skins.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-zucchini-boats/#wprm-recipe-52389-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/11/sausage-stuffed-zucchini-boats-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a pan saute the onions, garlic, and scooped zucchini on medium heat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-zucchini-boats/#wprm-recipe-52389-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/11/sausage-stuffed-zucchini-boats-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix in the spices.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-zucchini-boats/#wprm-recipe-52389-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/11/sausage-stuffed-zucchini-boats-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Turn the heat up to medium-high, then add in the ground pork.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-zucchini-boats/#wprm-recipe-52389-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/11/sausage-stuffed-zucchini-boats-05.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the pork has cooked, mix in your cheese, cooking until it melts. Divide the cooked zucchini and pork mixture equally among the zucchini shells.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-zucchini-boats/#wprm-recipe-52389-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/11/sausage-stuffed-zucchini-boats-07.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Top with some more cheese and place into a casserole dish.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-zucchini-boats/#wprm-recipe-52389-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/11/sausage-stuffed-zucchini-boats-08.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour a ½ cup of chicken broth into the bottom of the dish.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-zucchini-boats/#wprm-recipe-52389-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/11/sausage-stuffed-zucchini-boats-09.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 30 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/sausage-zucchini-boats/#wprm-recipe-52389-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": null
    }
